# One Rust core — zero wrapper drift

**JS, Python, and Rust wrappers must behave the same because they call the
same `xpict-core` code.** There is no expected drift to “keep in sync” by
reimplementing logic per language. Drift means a host grew a parallel engine;
fix that by moving the logic into Rust.

## Python / JS hosts

**Types + language-specific adapters only.** Not inherently language-specific
logic goes in Rust.

Allowed: generated contracts (`make types`), thin `_native` / wasm calls,
IPython/`_repr_*_` / DOM presentation, Chematic or other host-only I/O,
packaging.

Forbidden: cascade, paint, layout, align, compose, edge plan, DepictSpec
semantics, or any algorithm that belongs in `xpict-core` — including
“temporary” host copies.

## When adding a feature

1. Implement and test in Rust (`xpict-core`).
2. Expose the same API through bindings.
3. Hosts: types + call Rust. Never a second implementation.
